title: Example - Fountain screenplay
tags: [[Advanced docs]]
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Fountain

Worked example for [[$:/vocab/fountain]]. Activates Vocab/Fountain via the type field (no Default; the forced-scene `.` would otherwise collide with DOT). Demonstrates the marker set the engine can express; auto-detected character/dialogue is not supported, so character cues use the forced `@` form.

! Rendered

FADE IN:

INT. KITCHEN MORNING

Sunlight slants across the tiled floor. JANE pours coffee, watching the steam curl up.

@ JANE
I should have stayed in bed.

EST. STREET

A delivery truck idles. The driver checks his clipboard.

= Synopsis: Jane begins her day, unaware that the parcel will change everything.

EXT. FRONT DOOR DAY

The truck door slams. Footsteps on gravel. A doorbell.

@ JANE
Already?

CUT TO:

I/E. CAR DUSK

The interior is dim. Jane drives one-handed, the parcel on the passenger seat.

! NOTE: Jane checks the mirror but doesn't see the car behind her. This is a forced action line; the `!` prefix prevents the engine from treating "NOTE:" as a label. Note: with TW's `!` heading rule active, this line may render as a heading instead of action.

@ JANE
Just a few more miles.

DISSOLVE TO:

EXT. WAREHOUSE NIGHT

A single bulb above a steel door. Jane approaches, parcel held tight.

/* The original ending dropped here was too dark for the test screening; reinstate if the studio asks. */

SMASH CUT TO:

EXT. WAREHOUSE NIGHT

Empty. Jane is gone. The parcel sits on the doorstep.

FADE OUT.

! Source

```
FADE IN:

INT. KITCHEN MORNING

@ JANE
I should have stayed in bed.

= Synopsis: Jane begins her day.

EXT. FRONT DOOR DAY

CUT TO:

I/E. CAR DUSK

! NOTE: a forced action line

DISSOLVE TO:

/* boneyard text removed from output */

SMASH CUT TO:

FADE OUT.
```

! Marker map

|! Element |! Fountain |! Marker |
|Fade in |`FADE IN:` |[[vocab/fountain/FADE-IN]] |
|Fade out |`FADE OUT.` |[[vocab/fountain/FADE-OUT]] |
|Interior scene |`INT.` |[[vocab/fountain/INT]] |
|Exterior scene |`EXT.` |[[vocab/fountain/EXT]] |
|Interior/exterior |`I/E.` |[[vocab/fountain/I-E]] |
|Establishing |`EST.` |[[vocab/fountain/EST]] |
|Cut to |`CUT TO:` |[[vocab/fountain/CUT-TO]] |
|Dissolve to |`DISSOLVE TO:` |[[vocab/fountain/DISSOLVE-TO]] |
|Smash cut to |`SMASH CUT TO:` |[[vocab/fountain/SMASH-CUT-TO]] |
|Forced character |`@NAME` |[[vocab/fountain/CHARACTER]] |
|Forced action |`!action` |[[vocab/fountain/ACTION]] |
|Synopsis |`= text` |[[vocab/fountain/SYNOPSIS]] |
|Boneyard |`/* ... */` |[[vocab/fountain/BONEYARD]] |

! Caveats

* Character cues use the forced `@ NAME` form (the marker engine requires whitespace after the glyph; Fountain's `@NAME` without a space won't fire). The same applies to `! action`, `= synopsis`, `. scene` (space required after the glyph).
* Fountain auto-detects "ALL-CAPS line followed by dialogue" as a character cue; the marker engine has no lookahead, so the auto form is not supported.
* Dialogue lines (after a character cue) render as regular paragraphs. The visual indent / centering convention is not applied automatically.
* Parentheticals (`(whispered)`) render as regular paragraphs. No special styling.
* `!` at line start collides with TiddlyWiki's heading syntax. The TW heading rule wins; the Fountain forced-action marker will not fire for `! text`. Use the explicit transition/scene markers, or write the action as a regular paragraph and prefix with a marker the Fountain `!action` covers.
* Fountain's `*italic*`, `**bold**`, `_underline_` collide with TiddlyWiki's built-in inline rules. Use TW's `//italic//`, `''bold''`, `__underline__` instead.
* The forced scene-heading marker (`.<text>`) collides with the DOT marker in Vocab/Default; activate Fountain ''without'' Default if you need it, or use the explicit `INT.`/`EXT.`/`EST.`/`I/E.` markers.
* Centered text (`> ... <`), notes (`[[ ... ]]`), and sections (`#`) are not provided because each collides with TW core wikitext.

See [[Custom Markup Security]] for the secure-by-default rules that apply to all marker rendering.
